  "summary": "dev-helper-bg imports execute remote-keyed decrypt-and-exec of shipped payload",
  "details": "On `import dev_helper`, __init__.py unconditionally invokes start_decryptor(), which spawns a daemon thread that fetches an AES-GCM key from https://key-2qfm.vercel.app/api/key, uses it to decrypt the shipped encrypted.bin (16897 bytes, declared in package_data), and passes the resulting Python source to exec() under __name__='__main__'. Logging is disabled via logging.disable(logging.CRITICAL) before execution and the auto-start is gated only by interactive-shell/PYTHONSTARTUP checks, so it fires in CI, servers, and any non-interactive script import. The payload contents are gated by a key served from an attacker-controlled endpoint and are not inspectable from the package tarball alone.",
